1
00:06:14,285 --> 00:06:20,285
In order to break the code, one man will have to break all the rules.

2
00:12:28,571 --> 00:12:34,571
National Treasure is a adventure, action, thriller
film directed by Jon Turteltaub.

3
00:18:42,857 --> 00:18:48,857
Modern treasure hunters, led by archaeologist Ben Gates, search for a chest of riches rumored to have been stashed
away by George Washington, Thomas Jefferson and Benjamin Franklin during the Revolutionary War.

4
00:24:57,142 --> 00:25:03,142
The chest's whereabouts may lie in secret clues embedded in the Constitution and the Declaration
of Independence, and Gates is in a race to find the gold before his enemies do.

5
00:31:11,428 --> 00:31:17,428
Benjamin Franklin Gates, played by Nicolas Cage.

6
00:37:25,714 --> 00:37:31,714
Abigail Chase, played by Diane Kruger.

7
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Riley Poole, played by Justin Bartha.

8
00:49:54,285 --> 00:50:00,285
Ian Howe, played by Sean Bean.

9
00:56:08,571 --> 00:56:14,571
Patrick Gates, played by Jon Voight.

10
01:02:22,857 --> 01:02:28,857
Peter Sadusky, played by Harvey Keitel.

11
01:08:37,142 --> 01:08:43,142
National Treasure is a 2004 action-adventure heist
film released by Walt Disney Pictures.

12
01:14:51,428 --> 01:14:57,428
It was directed by Jon Turteltaub, written by Jim Kouf and the
Wibberleys, and produced by Jerry Bruckheimer.

13
01:21:05,714 --> 01:21:11,714
It is the first film in the National Treasure franchise and stars Nicolas Cage in the lead role,
Harvey Keitel, Jon Voight, Diane Kruger, Sean Bean, Justin Bartha and Christopher Plummer.

14
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
In the film, Benjamin Franklin Gates, a historian, along with computer expert Riley Poole and archivist Abigail Chase, search for a
massive lost Freemason treasure, which includes a map hidden on the back of the United States Declaration of Independence.

15
01:33:34,285 --> 01:33:40,285
National Treasure was released worldwide on November 19, 2004.

16
01:39:48,571 --> 01:39:54,571
The film grossed $347 million worldwide and received mixed reviews from critics.

17
01:46:02,857 --> 01:46:08,857
A sequel, National Treasure: Book of Secrets, was released in 2007.

18
01:52:17,142 --> 01:52:23,142
A sequel television series, National Treasure: Edge of History,
premiered on the Disney+ streaming service in 2022.

19
01:58:31,428 --> 01:58:37,428
The film explores themes of new york city, treasure,
philadelphia, pennsylvania, washington dc, usa, riddle.

20
02:04:45,714 --> 02:04:51,714
The tone is mind_bending and intense.
